WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:08.701
This tutorial shows what the Crewflow Dashboard tells you, and how its figures

2
00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:13.350
behave. Everything you see uses fictional demonstration data.

3
00:00:13.807 --> 00:00:16.736
Select Dashboard in the sidebar.

4
00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:24.756
As the data arrives, each number counts up to its value, and the bars and fills grow

5
00:00:24.756 --> 00:00:28.934
into place. The whole reveal takes just over a second.

6
00:00:29.394 --> 00:00:35.282
The strip at the top splits your current offers into pending, accepted by staff, and

7
00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:41.029
confirmed by a manager. Open shifts is the share of shifts in the next thirty days

8
00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:42.431
that are still open.

9
00:00:42.897 --> 00:00:49.600
Beside it are your totals: Staff, the Venue managers in your workspace, and your

10
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.186
Venues.

11
00:00:50.641 --> 00:00:56.708
Hours worked adds up completed attendance for each of the last seven days. The large

12
00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:01.764
figure is the daily average, across the days that have recorded hours.

13
00:01:02.226 --> 00:01:07.735
Shifts by venue counts the last thirty days of shifts at your busiest venues.

14
00:01:08.186 --> 00:01:13.574
Shift readiness follows your next shift in the coming fourteen days, from staffing

15
00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:16.859
and attendance through to the finalised timesheet.

16
00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:22.850
Further down, the offer pipeline breaks your current offers down by stage, and the

17
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.565
week view lists this week's shifts with their staffing.

18
00:01:27.031 --> 00:01:33.457
Now open Users, and select the Venue managers tab. This is the same list of Venue

19
00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:36.234
managers that the Dashboard counts.

20
00:01:36.686 --> 00:01:43.485
Return to the Dashboard. Because you came back on purpose, the figures replay their

21
00:01:43.485 --> 00:01:44.550
short reveal.

22
00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:51.309
Crewflow also refreshes these figures in the background when something changes, for

23
00:01:51.309 --> 00:01:57.684
example when a staff member accepts an offer. When the values are unchanged, nothing

24
00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.961
moves, so the page stays calm.

25
00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:06.257
If a figure cannot be loaded, or is not available to you, it shows a dash rather

26
00:02:06.257 --> 00:02:12.100
than a zero. And if your device is set to reduce motion, the final values appear

27
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.122
straight away.

28
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:18.997
To go deeper, select the arrow on any card to open the page behind it.
